    "result_text": "I've completed my investigation. Here's what I found.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change described in the specification is **already fully implemented** in the codebase, and the test suite is **green** (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures). I verified rather than re-implementing, since fabricating edits over working code would be wrong.\n\n### What's in place\n\nEvery rejection path for the in-scope statuses routes through an escalation handler in `src/main/java/.../rest/escalation/`, and each builds an RFC7807 body via the shared `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper, which sets all four required members:\n- `type` \u2192 `about:blank` (RFC7807 default)\n- `title` \u2192 exception simple name\n- `status` \u2192 via `ProblemDetail.forStatus(status)`\n- `detail` \u2192 human-readable message\n\nCoverage by status:\n- **400** \u2014 `DisposableEmail`, `InvalidPostcode`, `Validation` (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`), `FutureRegistrationDate`, `InvalidEmail`, `MissingOwnerFields`, `InvalidTelephone`\n- **409** \u2014 `CityAtCapacity`, `DuplicateIdentity`\n- **429** \u2014 `DailyLimitExceeded`\n\nHTTP status codes are unchanged (each handler still returns its original status via `ResponseEntity.status(...)`).\n\n### Verification performed\n\n1. **New test passes** \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` (POST `/api/owners` missing `city` \u2192 400) asserts `content().contentTypeCompatibleWith(\"application/problem+json\")` and `$.status == 400`; it passes.\n2. **No out-of-band rejections** \u2014 grepping the main source for `BAD_REQUEST`/`CONFLICT`/`TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`/`.status(...)` outside `escalation/` finds only success/redirect responses (201/204/302), so nothing bypasses the problem+json handlers.\n3. **Content type** \u2014 the 409/429 handlers use the identical `ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>>` construct as the verified 400 path; OfficeFloor derives `application/problem+json` from the `ProblemDetail` body type, so they serialize the same way.\n4. **Full suite** \u2014 `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nNo code changes were needed \u2014 the specification and all existing and new tests are already satisfied.",
